    {
      "type": "instruction",
      "text": "Principle 5. At school"
    },
    {
      "type": "sentences",
      "items": [
        {
          "n": "48",
          "text": "I'm often late for school because I sleep in late."
        },
        {
          "n": "49",
          "text": "My family is so busy we can't even eat breakfast together."
        },
        {
          "n": "50",
          "text": "I usually walk to school."
        },
        {
          "n": "51",
          "text": "It takes about 15 minutes."
        },
        {
          "n": "52",
          "text": "Sometimes in spring or fall, I ride my bike to school."
        },
        {
          "n": "53",
          "text": "I usually get to school at 8:30."
        },
        {
          "n": "54",
          "text": "On my way to school I sometimes stop at the stationery store to buy"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "the supplies for class."
    },
    {
      "type": "sentences",
      "items": [
        {
          "n": "55",
          "text": "Our teacher calls roll before class starts."
        },
        {
          "n": "56",
          "text": "She also gives us the announcements for the day."
        },
        {
          "n": "57",
          "text": "Our classes start at 9 o'clock."
        },
        {
          "n": "58",
          "text": "When class starts, our teacher checks our homework first."
        },
        {
          "n": "59",
          "text": "Our class has a lot of smart students."
        },
        {
          "n": "60",
          "text": "So this makes us very competitive."
        },
        {
          "n": "61",
          "text": "But our classmates are very friendly towards one another."
        }
      ]
    },
